0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(The operational heart of CivicPulse is the status workflow. A report starts as reported, then) Tj
0 -16 Td
(can be moved to verified or rejected by a verifier or admin. The status rules are centralized in) Tj
0 -16 Td
(app/status_flow.py so the status logic is consistent and not scattered across routes. For) Tj
0 -16 Td
(example, a report cannot move to an invalid status, cannot jump around the workflow, and cannot) Tj
0 -16 Td
(be reassigned improperly once work has started.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(The allowed transitions are reported -> verified or rejected; verified -> assigned; assigned ->) Tj
0 -16 Td
(in_progress; in_progress -> resolved. Final states are rejected and resolved. Rejections require) Tj
0 -16 Td
(a note explaining why the report is invalid. Once a report is assigned, it cannot be reassigned) Tj
0 -16 Td
(as long as the work has started in_progress. This is enforced by the reassign logic and the) Tj
0 -16 Td
(business rule that in-progress reports are protected from reassignment.) Tj
0 -16 Td
